[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Space Odyssey]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.85]Lesson 35 | 第35课
[00:03.08]Space odyssey | 太空探险
[00:11.10]When will it be possible for us to think seriously about colonising Mars? | 什么时候我们才有可能认真考虑移民火星？
[00:19.13]The Moon is likely to become the industrial hub of the Solar System supplying the rocket fuels for its ships, | 月球很可能成为太阳系的工业中心，为宇宙飞船供应火箭燃料，
[00:27.37]easily obtainable from the lunar rocks in the form of liquid oxygen. | 这种燃料极易从月球岩石中以液态氧的形式提取。
[00:33.54]The reason lies in its gravity. | 原因在于月球的重力。
[00:36.79]Because the Moon has only an eightieth of the Earth's mass, | 由于月球的质量只有地球的八十分之一，
[00:41.43]it requires 97% less energy | 所需能量要少97%，
[00:46.02]to travel the quarter of a million miles from the Moon to Earth-orbit than the 200 mile-journey from Earth's surface into orbit! | 从月球到地球轨道这25万英里的旅程，比从地球表面进入轨道那200英里的旅程还要省！
[00:57.44]This may sound fantastic, but it is easily calculated. | 这听起来也许离奇，但很容易计算出来。
[01:03.17]To escape from the Earth in a rocket, one must travel at seven miles per second. | 乘火箭脱离地球，必须达到每秒7英里的速度。
[01:10.27]The comparable speed from the Moon is only 1.5 miles per second. | 而从月球起飞相应的速度只有每秒1.5英里。
[01:17.34]Because the gravity on the Moon's surface is only a sixth of Earth's (remember how easily the Apollo astronauts bounded along), | 因为月球表面的重力只有地球的六分之一（想想阿波罗宇航员蹦蹦跳跳多么轻松），
[01:27.97]it takes much less energy to accelerate to that 1.5mps than it does on Earth. | 加速到每秒1.5英里所需的能量比在地球上少得多。
[01:36.60]Moon dwellers will be able to fly in space at only three percent of the cost of similar journeys by their terrestrial cousins. | 月球居民作太空飞行的费用，只相当于地球上的堂兄弟们同类旅程的3%。
[01:47.18]Arthur C.Clark once suggested a revolutionary idea passes through three phases: | 阿瑟·克拉克曾经提出，一个革命性的想法要经过三个阶段：
[01:55.37]1.  'It's impossible--don't waste my time.' | 1.“不可能——别浪费我的时间。”
[02:01.45]2.  'It's possible, but not worth doing.' | 2.“可能，但不值得做。”
[02:07.21]3.  'I said it was a good idea all along.' | 3.“我早就说过这是个好主意。”
[02:12.06]The idea of colonising Mars--a world 160 times more distant than the Moon--will move decisively from the second phase to the third, | 移民火星的想法——一个比月球远160倍的世界——将果断地从第二阶段转入第三阶段，
[02:25.21]when a significant number of people are living permanently in space. | 当相当多的人永久生活于太空之时。
[02:30.48]Mars has an extraordinary fascination for would-be voyagers. | 火星对未来的旅行者有着非同寻常的吸引力。
[02:35.77]America, Russia and Europe are filled with enthusiasts--many of them serious and senior scientists who dream of sending people to it. | 美国、俄国和欧洲到处是热心人——其中许多是严肃而资深的科学家，他们梦想把人送上火星。
[02:48.64]Their aim is understandable. | 他们的目的是可以理解的。
[02:51.22]It is the one world in the Solar System that is most like the Earth. | 它是太阳系中与地球最相似的一个世界。
[02:56.19]It is a world of red sandy deserts (hence its name--the Red Planet), | 它是一个由红色沙漠构成的世界（因此得名——红色行星），
[03:02.61]cloudless skies, savage sandstorms, chasms wider than the Grand Canyon and at least one mountain more than twice as tall as Everest. | 无云的天空、狂暴的沙暴、比大峡谷还宽的裂谷，以及至少一座比珠穆朗玛峰高两倍多的山峰。
[03:14.93]It seems ideal for settlement. | 它似乎是理想的定居地。
